hifiberry-bluetooth (1.0.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Set JustWorksRepairing = always in /etc/bluetooth/main.conf on configure.
    BlueZ has defaulted this to "never" since 5.51, which makes bluetoothd
    reject any re-pairing attempt from a device it still holds a link key
    for. That is the common case when a phone is reset, reinstalled, or
    simply told to forget the speaker: the phone offers a fresh pairing, the
    speaker refuses it, and neither side reports a useful error. The only
    way out is removing the device from the speaker over SSH or the WebUI.
    The setting is only added when no JustWorksRepairing value is active, so
    an explicit choice by the administrator is preserved, and it is removed
    again on purge.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-bluetooth (1.0.7) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add Breaks: hifiberry-audiocontrol (<< 0.8.8). Older audiocontrol still
    carries this player's inline entry in audiocontrol.json; combined with
    the /etc/audiocontrol/players.d/bluetooth.json conffile shipped since
    1.0.6, that duplicates into two BluetoothPlayerController instances
    against the same BlueZ D-Bus interface, since audiocontrol merges
    includes without deduplicating against the legacy players array.

